      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Another “No Name Given” CDL issued by California, contributing to 150+ arrests.  The El Centro Sector is taking aggressive action to combat the severe threat posed by unqualified commercial drivers on our roads. Tragic incidents, like the recent fatal crash in Indiana, highlight the catastrophic consequences when individuals not properly vetted or qualified operate 80,000-pound vehicles.  In the last four months, our agents have apprehended a staggering 172 individuals with Commercial Driver’s Licenses who lacked legal authorization to be here in the U.S. 118 of them issued by California. These arrests span numerous nationalities, including 96 from India, 14 from El Salvador, 13 from China, and others from countries like Tajikistan, Eritrea, and Turkey, demonstrating the widespread nature of this threat.  #CBP #DHS #BorderPatrol #CommercialDrivers",
      "text_resolved": "Another “No Name Given” CDL issued by California, contributing to 150+ arrests.  The El Centro Sector is taking aggressive action to combat the severe threat posed by unqualified commercial drivers on our roads. Tragic incidents, like the recent fatal crash in Indiana, highlight the catastrophic consequences when individuals not properly vetted or qualified operate 80,000-pound vehicles.  In the last four months, our agents have apprehended a staggering 172 individuals with Commercial Driver’s Licenses who lacked legal authorization to be here in the U.S. 118 of them issued by California. These arrests span numerous nationalities, including 96 from India, 14 from El Salvador, 13 from China, and others from countries like Tajikistan, Eritrea, and Turkey, demonstrating the widespread nature of this threat.  #CBP #DHS #BorderPatrol #CommercialDrivers",
